        "expression": "sum(history*(k0*exp(times[0]/tau)+k1*exp(times[1]/tau)+k2*exp(times[2]/tau)+k3*exp(times[3]/tau)))",
        "interpretation": "Dimensionless-scale contribution to response from prior drive history, with separate fitted weights for each lag interval and exponential waiting-time decay.",
        "name": "history_effect"
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "The old state-only response misses history-dependent contrasts, and the supplied C5/C6 models with a single discounted summary retain substantial dev error. This replacement allows each of the four history positions to have its own fitted weight while preserving explicit current-drive and waiting-time effects. Because coefficients are refit on fit rows and the history values there vary broadly, the model tests whether lag position matters without presuming a specific unique mechanism. The dev and matched-history observations show strong response changes with history and waiting time; the fresh observations add matched-u, matched-h lag contrasts. No dev RMSE is supplied for this proposed model, so passing the 0.06 criterion is not established until evaluation.",
    "scientific_change": "Replace a single exponential history summary with a flexible four-lag weighted history response whose weights share an exponential time-decay scale, allowing distinct contributions from prior intervals while retaining additive current drive and waiting-time terms."
  },
